Poo?<P>I'm only speaking for myself, the grumpy gnome here.  <IMG SRC="smile.gif" border="0"><P>Maybe i'm just jaded, but I have had NO interest to log into EQ since I bought and installed DAoC.  I don't plan to cancel my account, but I think alot of us are just tired of EQ.  Sure, DAoC is the shiny new toy to play with, but i'm actually enjoying playing it, whereas EQ became nothing but a second job.  In the high-end game if you aren't in a guild doing high-end encounters there isn't really anything you can just log on and do.  Add in the fact that I've seen everything there is to see in EQ except for Plane of Mischief it just isn't as "cool" as it used to be.  /shrug  Being a complete newbie in DAoC kinda reminds me of how I felt when I started EQ.  Not knowing what would kick my rear in 2 seconds, not knowing what exactly was beyond the next corner, etc etc.  DAoC does have some issues I think, but I'm willing to overlook them just like I overlooked many of EQs' faults.  Not everyone feels the same way about EQ as I do, but i'm having fun with my new toy, and not my old one.  <P>Ta Ta, see you in DAoC possibly,<P>--------------------<P>Wardak - 7th Level Norseman Warrior<BR>Gawaine Server<BR>Kruunk - 11th Level Firbolg Hero<BR>Galahad Server<P>Lownar, Kalaan, Rakasak - Retired
